      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61c178e1d585bf0b4b2b6fb9|full_name} Yeah, we've been using that and it's a start, but it's failing in two important ways I want to make sure are addressed in the ticket\n\nFirst, that only affects user uploaded emoji, not the default VRChat included ones\n\nSecond, if you hit \"Show Avatar\" on a person it will override that setting for that person, which again may accidentally allow emotes by a person who is unaware of another person's photosensitivity. It'll block you from having safety settings but \"I want to show this person cause I'm talking to them\" without opening up that risk\n\nHopefully it's not too much work to make that global setting you mentioned cover both those additional scenarios, it would be a huge help for some players",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
